      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T16:38:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I mean is, I don\u0027t think we can guarantee that the TCPC has not reset, even during a BIST test. Unless we can guarantee that it hasn\u0027t reset, we shouldn\u0027t set the return value of `register_mask_reset` to indicate that the TCPC hasn\u0027t reset. If we don\u0027t care whether the TCPC has reset, then we can decide not to call `register_mask_reset` based on `bist_mode`. If we do care whether the TCPC has reset, then we should do these 2 register reads.\n\nIf we do these 2 reads in BIST mode, does that by itself break the test? If the test still passes with these 2 reads, I\u0027d rather just leave this part of the code as is.",
